#{[17592186502109 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502109 #edb/ref 1069 "q-28288" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502109 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502109 #edb/ref 1071 "A line $l$ is parallel to $4x-2y=6.$ A possible equation for $l$ is" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502109 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63caf14b-4a45-5fc8-9446-996c19cf7a2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502109 #edb/ref 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $4x-2y=6,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2y & =6 \\\\ -2y & =-4x+6 \\\\ y & =2x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $2.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $2$ is $y=2x+6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502128 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502128 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44382" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502128 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502128 #edb/ref 1071 "A line $l$ is parallel to $4x-y=22.$  A possible equation for $l$ is" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502128 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9815706a-98d4-5baf-aff8-15181269835f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502128 #edb/ref 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $4x-y=22,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-y & =22 \\\\ -y & =-4x+22 \\\\ y & =4x-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $4.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $4$ is $y=4x+8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502137 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502137 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44380" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502137 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502137 #edb/ref 1071 "A line $l$ is parallel to $6x-2y=11.$ A possible equation for $l$ is" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502137 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b444fd71-00fa-57c3-8df1-8666ae2725d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502137 #edb/ref 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $6x-2y=11,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-2y & =11 \\\\ \\frac{6}{2}x-\\frac{2}{2}y & =\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ 3x-y & =\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ -y & =-3x+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ y & =3x-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $3.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $3$ is $y=3x-8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502163 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502163 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502163 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502163 #edb/ref 1071 "The lines $y=\\frac{8}{5}x+9$ and $y=mx+3$ are parallel. The value of $m=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502163 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9e5b1d4-9811-5c7c-998e-01070d311e7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186502163 #edb/ref 1074 "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nBoth lines are in slope-intercept form, so we can pick out the slope of each equation by looking at the $x$-coefficient.\n\n- The slope of the line $y=\\frac{8}{5}x+9$ is $\\frac{8}{5}.$\n\n- The slope of the line $y=mx+3$ is $m.$\n\nBecause the slopes must be the same, we must have $m=\\frac{8}{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
